-- The Indian Nutrient Databank, as this clinic's recipe library.
--
-- 1,014 recipes with their ingredients, from the INDB published by Jaacks et
-- al. (University of Edinburgh): https://github.com/lindsayjaacks/Indian-Nutrient-Databank-INDB-
-- Recipes are drawn from 'The Art & Science of Cooking' (490), 'Basic Food
-- Preparation' (378) and open web sources (148); ingredient composition comes
-- from ICMR-NIN IFCT, UK CoFID and USDA FoodData Central.
--
-- NOTHING HERE IS SELECTABLE ON A CLIENT'S CHART YET. Every dish arrives
-- unapproved, and the chart's recipe picker only offers approved ones. The
-- dietitian works through them in batches; until she does, this is a reference
-- library and nothing more.
--
-- TWO KINDS OF NUMBER, AND WHICH WINS
--
-- Where a recipe's ingredient weights are complete, the app computes its
-- figures the way it computes every other dish — ingredients, food table,
-- arithmetic. Where they are not, it falls back to INDB's own published
-- per-serving figures, which are marked as such on screen.
--
-- The gap is unit conversion, not effort. INDB records over half its
-- ingredient amounts in teaspoons, tablespoons, cups and sprigs; its own
-- conversion sheet covers some of those and not others, so 4,957 of 10,271
-- ingredient rows arrive with a weight and the rest arrive at zero. A recipe
-- with a zero-weight ingredient is not computable and says so. Each gram
-- conversion added later flips more recipes from published to computed,
-- without touching this file.
--
-- Deliberately no guessed weights. A teaspoon of salt and a teaspoon of
-- saffron are not the same mass, and a plausible number here would be
-- indistinguishable from a measured one everywhere downstream.

-- ---- 1. ingredients IFCT does not carry ----------------------------------
-- Salt, sugar, refined oils, spice blends, baking staples. IFCT covers raw
-- agricultural foods; a jar of garam masala is not one. Each row keeps the
-- name of the table it came from, so any figure on a chart stays traceable.
on conflict (food_code) do nothing;

-- ---- 2. the recipes -------------------------------------------------------
on conflict (source) do nothing;

